# FBIAS - Multiple Models Example

This example demonstrates how to aggregate CTS (contingency table statistics) data from
MET stat files for several ensemble members at once and plot frequency bias (FBIAS) for
each of them on the same chart using VCasT. It compares 10 members of the
`RRFS_GDAS_GF.SPP.SPPT` ensemble for 3-hr accumulated precipitation (APCP_03, >0.0 mm)
across lead time.

## Data Aggregation:
This step processes the MET CTS stat files for all 10 members and aggregates FBIAS into a
single output file, grouped by model/fcst_var/fcst_lead.

## Plot Generation:
This step uses the aggregated output file to plot one FBIAS line per model (the `unique`
list in `plot.yaml` splits the aggregated data by `model`).

## Commands

1. Aggregate Data
Run the following command to process the MET stat files. This produces `APCP_agg.data`.

```bash
# Aggregates MET CTS stat files for all models and creates the aggregated data file
vcast cts.yaml
```

2. Generate the FBIAS Plot
Once the data aggregation is complete, run the following command to generate the plot
using the aggregated data:

```bash
# Generates the multi-model FBIAS plot using the aggregated output file
vcast plot.yaml
```
